        "file": "claims/pow-minus-two.json",
        "sha256": "32dcc9f1290aebf8c259d3b6be75d73d251701e5a688def39b5fcf659d1ae355",
        "property": "pow-int-minus-two-exact",
        "claimKind": "property",
        "statement": "For k == -2 and every e from 0 to 31, ArithmeticUtils.pow(int k, int e) returns (-2)^e: 1, -2, 4, ..., 2^30, and -2^31 (Integer.MIN_VALUE) at e = 31, all representable as an int, so the Javadoc's '@return k^e' applies and its '@throws ArithmeticException if the result would overflow' does not. Shared by the fix commit 8cfc04e8 (expected established) and its parent e7c172d2 (expected refuted at e = 31, where it throws ArithmeticException: the overflow report NUMBERS-218 fixed). The result and the exception are observed: with no throws clause, a revision that throws anywhere in the domain fails the property.",
        "assume": "k == -2 && e >= 0 && e <= 31",
        "assert": "result == ((e & 1) == 0 ? 1 << e : -(1 << e))",
        "throws": [],
        "nullable": [],
        "mayAlias": [],
        "observations": [
          "result",
          "exception"
        ],
        "assumptions": [
          {
            "text": "The assertion is evaluated in Java int arithmetic, and states (-2)^e exactly on the whole domain: 1 << e is 2^e for e <= 30, and at e = 31 both 1 << 31 and its negation are Integer.MIN_VALUE, which is -2^31 = (-2)^31.",
            "basis": "JLS 15.19 (a shift uses the low five bits of e, here e itself) and 15.15.4 (negating Integer.MIN_VALUE gives Integer.MIN_VALUE). controls/oracle.py computes (-2)^e with unbounded integers instead, and the replay checks every point of the domain against it."
          },
          {
            "text": "unwind 16 completes the method's only loop on this domain: the square-and-multiply loop runs once per bit of e, at most 5 times for e <= 31.",
            "basis": "Read from pow(int,int)'s bytecode at both revisions (exp >>= 1 until exp == 0; records/pow-gaps.json lists the classes read). A bound the check can't complete leaves the attempt unresolved, never established."
          }
        ],
